From 82f97c92fb7b986e16befed1c0b30b770b27d99d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guillain d'Erceville <guillain@poulpe.us>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 10:42:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/grundig_sp: add Grundig DSS-SP (Digta CELP) decoder

Grundig DigtaSoft dictation devices store recordings in a DSS container
variant identified by the magic byte 6 ('\x06dss') and a fixed six-block
(6 x 512 byte) header.  Its audio payload is not the Olympus DSS-SP or
G.723.1 codec already supported by the dss demuxer, but a distinct CELP
coder (Digta SP), as produced and decoded by Grundig's dss2wav codec.

The codec operates at a native 12 kHz sampling rate.  Each 41-byte
(328-bit) frame yields 288 samples (4 subframes x 72).  A frame carries
14 reflection-coefficient indices feeding an order-14 lattice synthesis
filter, four differential pitch lags packed into a single 24-bit field
and, per subframe, an adaptive (pitch) gain, a 31-bit fixed-codebook
index that enumerates 7 pulses through cumulative binomial tables, a
fixed-codebook gain and 7 pulse signs.  The excitation is the sum of an
adaptive (pitch repetition x gain) and a fixed (7 signed pulses)
contribution; a de-emphasis filter (y[n] = x[n] + 0.1*y[n-1]) and
rounding/clamping to int16 follow.

The Grundig device resamples the 12 kHz signal to 16 kHz with a 3:4
polyphase FIR for playback.  That resampling is a device post-process
and is intentionally left to libswresample; the decoder emits the
codec's native 12 kHz rate.  The decoder uses f64 arithmetic and
floor(x + 0.5) rounding and is bit-exact against the reference codec.

The demuxer is extended to detect the '\x06dss' variant, expose a new
AV_CODEC_ID_GRUNDIG_SP stream at 12000 Hz, and emit the 41-byte frames
following the Grundig block rule (b2 frames start per block at the
(b1<<8|b0)>>4 bit offset, frames forming a continuous bitstream that
spans block boundaries).  The existing Olympus DSS-SP / G.723.1 paths
are untouched.

A framecrc FATE test (fate-dss-grundig-sp) is added.

Signed-off-by: Guillain d'Erceville <guillain@poulpe.us>
